  seen in the last six months alone there  were 1300 deaths every week over and  above what you would normally find covid  accounts for some of these debts but  according to health leaders most are  being caused by the crisis in the NHS  ambulance workers say they're fighting  for better pay and to improve patient  care  but industrial action puts more pressure  on a buckling NHS and almost certainly  more patient harm Ash's Joshi Sky News  Central London
 

